Define a class called Person:
    To initialize with name, age:
        Set this.name to name
        Set this.age to age

    Method get_name:
        Return this.name

    Method is_adult:
        Return this.age is at least 18

Define a class called Employee inheriting from Person:
    To initialize with name, age, title:
        Call parent with name, age
        Set this.title to title

    Method get_title:
        Return this.title

    Method introduce:
        Return this.name + " (" + this.title + ")"

Set p to a new Person with "Alice", 28
Assert(p.get_name() is equal to "Alice")
Assert(p.age is equal to 28)
Assert(p.is_adult() is equal to true)

Set p.age to 15
Assert(p.is_adult() is equal to false)

Set emp to a new Employee with "Bob", 35, "Principal Engineer"
Assert(emp.get_name() is equal to "Bob")
Assert(emp.get_title() is equal to "Principal Engineer")
Assert(emp.introduce() is equal to "Bob (Principal Engineer)")
Assert(emp.is_adult() is equal to true)

Assert(emp is an instance of Employee)
Assert(emp is an instance of Person)
Assert(p is an instance of Person)
Assert(p is not an instance of Employee)

Assert(type("hello") is equal to "string")
Assert(type(123) is equal to "int")
Assert(type(3.14) is equal to "float")
Assert(type(true) is equal to "bool")
Assert(type([1, 2]) is equal to "list")
Assert(type({"k": 1}) is equal to "map")
Assert(type(p) is equal to "instance")
Assert(type(Person) is equal to "class")

Assert("world" is a string)
Assert(42 is a number)
Assert(42 is an integer)
Assert(3.1415 is a float)
Assert(true is a boolean)
Assert([1, 2] is a list)
Assert({"a": 1} is a map)
Assert(p.get_name is a function)

Get regex
Assert(regex.is_match("^[a-z]+@[a-z]+\\.[a-z]+$", "alice@example.com") is equal to true)
Assert(regex.is_match("^[0-9]+$", "1234") is equal to true)
Assert(regex.is_match("^[0-9]+$", "12a4") is equal to false)
Assert(regex.find("\\d+", "Order 482 created") is equal to "482")
Assert(regex.replace("dog", "cat", "The dog barked") is equal to "The cat barked")
Assert(regex.split("\\s+", "Lyslyn is enterprise grade").length is equal to 4)

Get os
Set plat to os.platform()
Assert(plat is a string)
Assert(plat.length is greater than 0)
Set cur_dir to os.cwd()
Assert(cur_dir is a string)

Get math
Assert(math.sin(0) is equal to 0.0)
Assert(math.cos(0) is equal to 1.0)
Assert(math.hypot(3, 4) is equal to 5.0)

Get text
Assert(text.repeat("Lys", 3) is equal to "LysLysLys")
Assert(text.index_of("hello world", "world") is equal to 6)
Assert(text.pad_start("42", 5, "0") is equal to "00042")
Assert(text.char_at("Lyslyn", 0) is equal to "L")

Say "All Java and Python level language features verified successfully!"
